messages.content:
{
 "what_you_observe": [
  "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. Six am in the Hearthside Hotel. Three bright radio notes. A delivery van backfires twice.",
  "The crew meets for coffee at the hotel. The afternoon is open. A coat-check envelope holds the TV crew’s return fares. The party is at the ballroom tonight. A stranded driver needs a jack, and the ballroom piano is free.",
  "The Rialto is closing. The regional line can carry one last reel out of town. Alma wants her daughter in Pittsburgh to hear her voice.",
  "An envelope has arrived from Pittsburgh. Alma's daughter sent a receipt for a recorded interview. The line copied her reply: 'I know that voice. Play it again.'"
 ],
 "your_own_memories": [
  {
   "when": "last Tuesday afternoon",
   "witnessed": "Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh.."
  },
  {
   "when": "last evening in Pittsburgh",
   "witnessed": "You reached your sister from the terminal payphone. She confirmed the van booking for Wednesday.",
   "your_words": "Hey, it's Phil. I'm in Pittsburgh now, just off the coach. Listen, about tomorrow—van's booked for the couch, right? I want to nail down the pickup time and make sure I know which hallway we're dragging it through. I'll be at your place by noon, tops."
  },
  {
   "when": "this morning",
   "witnessed": "After that evening in Pittsburgh you woke back in your hotel bed. The radio again announced Tuesday, February 2."
  },
  {
   "afternoon": "Phil pockets the contents of the crew fare envelope. The envelope is empty.",
   "evening": "Phil lets the evening go by in bed alone.",
   "what_you_said": "Rita. I hear you. About Alma. I'll call her from the terminal tomorrow, after I'm off the coach. I'll ask her what she wants to hear. I'll just... listen. I'll do it from a payphone with a three-minute limit and I'll do it. Goodnight.",
   "your_last_intention": "Be on that coach at first light. Be in Pittsburgh by ten. Be at my sister's door by noon. Move the goddamn couch. That's the whole evening. That's the whole point of the week.",
   "next_wake": "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. Six am in the Hearthside Hotel. Three bright radio notes. A delivery van backfires twice."
  }
 ],
 "who_you_are_with": "Rita and Larry in the hotel lobby",
 "physical_choices": {
  "help_driver": "Use the afternoon to change a stranded driver's flat tire.",
  "rehearse_piano": "Spend the afternoon learning a tune at the ballroom piano.",
  "record_Alma": "Give the afternoon to recording Alma's account at the Rialto.",
  "take_coach": "Board your paid coach and physically reach Pittsburgh.",
  "stay_in_bed": "Close the curtains and spend the afternoon in bed.",
  "spend_time_here": "Stay in the hotel lobby.",
  "pocket_fare_envelope": "Take the cash from an unattended coat-check envelope marked CREW RETURN FARES. You can spend it tonight."
 }
}

{
  "action": "take_coach",
  "detail": "I push back from the coffee table. The paper cup is still warm. I set it down on the little saucer, not on the tablecloth, and stand. My coat is already on the back of the chair. I pull it over my shoulders, buttons to the third one, and walk to the lobby door. The door chime is a small, flat ding. I don't look back at the coffee. I don't look back at the coat-check desk where the envelope sits. I walk to the terminal lot. The coach is there, number plate dusty, engine ticking. I climb the steps. I put my ticket on the little shelf above the seat. I sit. The driver pulls the door shut. The engine turns over. The van backfires again, two notes, and the bus lurches forward into the road. I watch the hotel shrink in the mirror. I press my forehead to the glass for a second. Then I look forward. The windshield is clean. The road is straight. Pittsburgh is four hours away. I will be at my sister's door by eleven. The couch waits. The hallway is the short one, the one by the kitchen. I know this because I told her I'd confirm it and I did, last time, from the payphone, and she said, \"Yeah, short hall, by the kitchen, the couch faces the window.\" I'll be there. I'll be at the door. I'll say, \"I'm here, let's move this thing.\" And we will. That's the whole afternoon. That's the whole point.","intention": "Be on that coach. Be in Pittsburgh by ten. Be at my sister's door by noon. Move the couch. That's it. That's the whole thing. I will not sit in this bed tonight. I will not pocket that envelope. I will not call a number I don't need to call. I will be on the bus. I will be at the door. The couch will move. My sister will not have to move it alone.","words": "— I turn back to the lobby just long enough to say, flat, to nobody in particular, to the room, to the coffee, to the coat-check desk, to the man with the flat tire waiting by the van: \"I'm heading to Pittsburgh. Wednesday's the couch. I'll be there.\""
}
